  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Raju Laxmayya Kokonda vs State Of Maharashtra on 11 January, 2022 Author: C.V. Bhadang Bench: C.V. Bhadang 30 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Criminal Anticipatory Bail Application No.17 Of 2022 Raju Laxmayya Kokonda ... Vs. The State of Maharashtra ... ---- Mr.Rahul B. Vijaymane for the Applicant. Mr.R.M. Pethe, App for the Respondent -State. ---- Nilam Digitally signed by Nilam Santosh Coram : C.V. Bhadang, J. Santosh Kamble Date: 2022.01.11 Kamble 17:53:06 +0530 Date : 11 January 202 (Through Video Confer P.C. . The Applicant apprehending arrest in with investigation of Crime No.542 of 2021 registered wi Road Police Station under Section 3 and 26 of the Preven the Food Adulteration Act and Section 272 and 273 of the Indian Penal Code is seeking anticipatory bail. 2. The prosecution case is that from the the co-accused Satyanarayan Yeldi, 428 bottles of fruit Rs.12,840/- was seized.",
    "facts": "2. The prosecution case is that from the the co-accused Satyanarayan Yeldi, 428 bottles of fruit Rs.12,840/- was seized.",
    "arguments": "The learned counsel for the Applicant submitted that the Applicant has no role in the matter and the offence under Section 328 of IPC may not be made out. 4. The learned Additional Public Prosecutor has placed reliance on the decision of this Court in Vinod Ramnath Gupta V/s. State of Maharashtra1, which was a case of seizure of Gutka in order to submit that in such a case the offence under Section 328 of IPC can be made out. 5.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The learned counsel for the Applicant submitted that the Applicant has no role in the matter and the offence under Section 328 of IPC may not be made out. 4. The learned Additional Public Prosecutor has placed reliance on the decision of this Court in Vinod Ramnath Gupta V/s. State of Maharashtra1, which was a case of seizure of Gutka in order to submit that in such a case the offence under Section 328 of IPC can be made out. 5.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
